{"file":{"content":"viable and is complementary: exhibit from every state a block family of\nuntwisted mass $\\ge\\alpha$ whose endpoints contain a full coset of a subgroup\n$H$ with $\\chi|_H\\ne1$ (exact cancellation $\\sum_{u\\in H}\\chi(uh)=0$). For the\nkilled strip, build the families with identical valuation multisets so the\nheight weights match exactly, or prove bounded distortion\n$w_s(w_1)/w_s(w_2)\\in[C^{-1},C]$ with QSD bulk retention $O(e^{-cL})$.\n\n\\section*{Conclusion}\n\\addcontentsline{toc}{section}{Conclusion}\n\nThe defect cocycle relocates rather than removes the difficulty, but the\nfinite-operator side is now substantially a theorem. The rigorous core comprises\nthe sliding-window congruence; the proof that the quadratic character is\nvaluation parity in disguise, hence an exact coboundary; the \\emph{classification}\n$\\operatorname{Cob}=\\langle\\chi_2\\rangle$ (\\cref{thm:class}), which makes the\nnon-coboundary quotient canonical rather than conjectural; the strict spectral\ngap at every finite level (\\cref{cor:strict}); the conductor collapse\n(\\cref{thm:collapse}), which reduces uniformity in $Q$ to the single computable\nsequence $\\gamma_c(s)$; and the height-strip rotation identity\n(\\cref{prop:rot}). The remaining finite-operator task is exactly one statement,\n\\cref{conj:ext} (bounded-conductor extremality, $\\sup_c\\gamma_c<1$). The\nstability program of \\cref{sec:stability} reduces its polylog form to\ncomparison-graph expansion (\\cref{conj:exp}) via the proved extraction step\n\\cref{prop:stab}, with \\cref{lem:damp} identifying the coboundary modes as the\nonly undamped Fourier directions; descent (two scalar steps plus one rank-2\nstep, \\cref{thm:descent,thm:rank2}) makes the three deepest digits lossless,\nbut---an honest negative finding of this work---\\emph{stalls there}: rank\nsaturation fails, the internal classes refine by $\\times3$ per level, and the\nnonzero-eigenvalue count confirms there is no bounded-level reduction\n(\\cref{rem:saturation}). The canonical witness (\\cref{thm:witness}: two\nself-loops at level $9$, $W\\equiv4\\bmod9$) supplies full principal-unit\ngeneration and strict non-coboundarity on the audited range $c\\le c_0+3$. The\nquantitative heart that remains is \\cref{conj:ext} (bounded-conductor\nextremality), now supported additionally by the monotone decrease of the\nprimitive-sector radii in $c$; \\emph{short-witness coverage}\n(\\cref{conj:mult}) retains its conditional force but lacks, for now, a\nconstruction of bounded-level witnesses for large $c$. To be precise\nabout scope: it is the \\emph{finite H23a operator theorem} that reduces to\ncomparison-graph expansion---the global Collatz implication additionally\nrequires the quenched arrow (bad orbit $\\Rightarrow$ finite non-coboundary\nspectral shadow), which remains the open keystone.\n\n\\begin{thebibliography}{9}\n\\bibitem{companion} J.~A.~Janik, \\emph{Finite Spectral Shadows for the Collatz\nValuation Cocycle: computational companion}, accompanying numerical report (2026).\n\\end{thebibliography}\n\n\\end{document}\n","filePath":"/home/john/mynotes/deterministic_equidistribution_theory/finite_spectral_shadows.tex","numLines":49,"startLine":2040,"totalLines":2088},"type":"text"}